{"id": "state-look", "window": ["2016-10-24", "2022-12-30"], "intro": ["41,959 instrument-sessions, 34 instruments, London sessions 2018-04 to 2022-12 (fields need a year of M1 history first; M1 starts 2016-10). 2023 onward is not looked at. Every field uses only data from before the session; models are refitted each quarter on earlier sessions.", "The five fields are about two and a half, not five. The first principal component holds 61% of their variance and the second 22% (independent fields would be 20% each). σ now and σ vs long-run correlate 0.90; P(high regime) correlates 0.69 with σ now.", "σ alone is not flat across its own deciles: on the lowest-σ decile the session range is 1.86σ, on the highest 1.41σ (all-session mean 1.60σ). The live σ over-reacts: it is too high after loud spells and too low after quiet ones.", "Forecast error is the field that adds most beyond σ: top-decile minus bottom-decile range is +0.39σ [+0.29, +0.48] (shuffled field −0.03σ). Positive in all 5 years (+0.23 to +0.39 by fifths) and all 4 classes. P(high regime) adds nothing beyond σ (+0.02σ [−0.09, +0.15]); expected change adds little (+0.07σ, interval crosses 0).", "As a forecast of the session's 5-min realised variance, log-HAR on M1 beats the live σ: QLIKE 0.77 [0.73, 0.81] of the live σ's loss, below 1 in every year and every instrument, but only 0.96-0.97 on EURUSD, NZDUSD and USDCAD. On the squared-range yardstick (no home advantage) HAR is 0.89. σ × the error feedback is 0.92 [0.87, 0.96]. Fitted daily GARCH(1,1) is worse than the live σ (1.17).", "Expected change does point the right way: correlation 0.38 with next week's change in vol, against 0.21 for plain mean reversion (−σ vs long-run).", "For stops: a 1σ stop from the open is reached on 29.6% of sessions. When recent sessions ran hotter than σ (top two fifths of the error) it is 32-33%; when they ran cooler, 25-28%. The width hit on 20% of days goes from 1.13σ to 1.43σ across error deciles, against one width of 1.26σ for all days. The regime probability barely moves either.", "Descriptive only: deciles are over the whole window, nothing is scored as a trade, and costs are not in. The state's job here looks like resizing σ (error and level), not naming a regime."], "charts": [{"type": "lines", "title": "How long each field persists: autocorrelation by lag", "unit": "autocorrelation", "xlabel": "lag (sessions)", "note": "Average over 34 instruments, 2018-2022. Benchmark: a shuffled field is 0 at every lag. Realised log RV5 (the raw thing) is the reference for 'how sticky is vol itself'. Not drawn: Δσ expected (0.88 at lag 1, 0.13 at 20) and σ vs long-run (0.95, 0.51), which tracks σ now.", "series": [{"name": "σ now", "points": [[1, 0.955], [2, 0.933], [3, 0.909], [5, 0.856], [10, 0.705], [20, 0.525], [40, 0.346], [60, 0.207]]}, {"name": "P(high regime)", "points": [[1, 0.948], [2, 0.888], [3, 0.834], [5, 0.751], [10, 0.603], [20, 0.467], [40, 0.388], [60, 0.293]]}, {"name": "forecast error", "points": [[1, 0.981], [2, 0.948], [3, 0.905], [5, 0.806], [10, 0.559], [20, 0.253], [40, 0.047], [60, 0.012]]}, {"name": "realised log RV5", "points": [[1, 0.729], [2, 0.663], [3, 0.624], [5, 0.611], [10, 0.501], [20, 0.375], [40, 0.26], [60, 0.205]]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "How much the five fields overlap: correlation of each pair", "unit": "correlation", "ref": 0, "note": "Within-instrument z-scores, 2018-2022, 34 instruments pooled. Benchmark: shuffling rows gives |r| ≤ 0.011. Above ~0.7 the two fields carry the same information.", "rows": [{"label": "σ now vs Δσ expected", "value": -0.598}, {"label": "σ now vs σ vs long-run", "value": 0.899}, {"label": "σ now vs P(high regime)", "value": 0.694}, {"label": "σ now vs forecast error", "value": 0.026}, {"label": "Δσ expected vs σ vs long-run", "value": -0.594}, {"label": "Δσ expected vs P(high regime)", "value": -0.564}, {"label": "Δσ expected vs forecast error", "value": -0.4}, {"label": "σ vs long-run vs P(high regime)", "value": 0.612}, {"label": "σ vs long-run vs forecast error", "value": 0.063}, {"label": "P(high regime) vs forecast error", "value": 0.177}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Degrees of freedom: share of the five fields' variance on each principal component", "unit": "% of variance", "ref": 20, "note": "If the five fields were independent each component would hold 20% (the reference line). Components holding well under 20% add little new information.", "rows": [{"label": "component 1", "value": 60.8}, {"label": "component 2", "value": 22.2}, {"label": "component 3", "value": 8.4}, {"label": "component 4", "value": 6.8}, {"label": "component 5", "value": 1.8}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Session range ÷ σ by decile of each field", "unit": "high-low ÷ σ", "xlabel": "decile of the field (1 = lowest, within instrument)", "note": "If σ alone were enough, every line would sit flat at the all-session mean 1.60. A slope means the field knows something σ does not. Deciles over the whole window (descriptive, not a rule). Δσ expected is in the next chart.", "series": [{"name": "σ now", "points": [[1, 1.863], [2, 1.707], [3, 1.679], [4, 1.634], [5, 1.577], [6, 1.571], [7, 1.525], [8, 1.518], [9, 1.486], [10, 1.405]]}, {"name": "σ vs long-run", "points": [[1, 1.88], [2, 1.71], [3, 1.643], [4, 1.628], [5, 1.57], [6, 1.579], [7, 1.532], [8, 1.495], [9, 1.492], [10, 1.437]]}, {"name": "P(high regime)", "points": [[1, 1.623], [2, 1.609], [3, 1.609], [4, 1.611], [5, 1.584], [6, 1.583], [7, 1.563], [8, 1.569], [9, 1.571], [10, 1.646]]}, {"name": "forecast error", "points": [[1, 1.426], [2, 1.484], [3, 1.54], [4, 1.547], [5, 1.568], [6, 1.582], [7, 1.634], [8, 1.666], [9, 1.708], [10, 1.813]]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Top decile minus bottom decile of each field: session range ÷ σ", "unit": "Δ (high-low ÷ σ)", "ref": 0, "note": "95% date-block bootstrap. Benchmark: a shuffled field (last row) and 0. A positive bar: when the field is high, σ under-states the day's range.", "rows": [{"label": "σ now", "value": -0.4576, "lo": -0.5878, "hi": -0.3396}, {"label": "Δσ expected", "value": 0.072, "lo": -0.0838, "hi": 0.2198}, {"label": "σ vs long-run", "value": -0.4435, "lo": -0.5739, "hi": -0.2987}, {"label": "P(high regime)", "value": 0.0228, "lo": -0.0857, "hi": 0.1521}, {"label": "forecast error", "value": 0.3872, "lo": 0.2948, "hi": 0.4786}, {"label": "shuffled field (benchmark)", "value": -0.0254, "lo": -0.0864, "hi": 0.0309}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Forecast loss against the live σ: QLIKE ratio, all 34 instruments, 2018-2022", "unit": "QLIKE ÷ live σ", "ref": 1, "note": "Below 1 = a better forecast of the session's 5-min realised variance than the live σ. Every forecast is put on the RV5 scale with a past-only expanding mean, so this is shape, not level. 95% date-block bootstrap. Yesterday's RV is the naive benchmark.", "rows": [{"label": "log-HAR on RV5", "value": 0.773, "lo": 0.7327, "hi": 0.8127}, {"label": "GARCH(1,1), variance-targeted", "value": 1.1743, "lo": 1.0144, "hi": 1.3966}, {"label": "GARCH(1,1), free MLE", "value": 1.1988, "lo": 1.0306, "hi": 1.4359}, {"label": "σ × error feedback (F5)", "value": 0.9194, "lo": 0.8689, "hi": 0.9632}, {"label": "yesterday's RV (random walk)", "value": 0.9245, "lo": 0.8192, "hi": 1.0368}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "Same race, two yardsticks: 5-min realised variance vs squared session range", "names": ["target RV5", "target range²"], "unit": "QLIKE ÷ live σ", "note": "HAR is fitted on RV5, so it has home advantage on the RV5 yardstick. The squared high-low of the session is a separate proxy (both are valid for QLIKE up to scale). If a model wins on both, it is not just matching its own measure. Benchmark: 1 = live σ.", "rows": [{"label": "log-HAR on RV5", "values": [0.773, 0.8923]}, {"label": "GARCH(1,1), variance-targeted", "values": [1.1743, 1.0794]}, {"label": "GARCH(1,1), free MLE", "values": [1.1988, 1.0912]}, {"label": "σ × error feedback (F5)", "values": [0.9194, 0.9711]}, {"label": "yesterday's RV (random walk)", "values": [0.9245, 0.974]}]}, {"type": "groups", "title": "QLIKE ÷ live σ, year by year", "names": ["log-HAR on RV5", "GARCH(1,1), variance-targeted", "σ × error feedback (F5)"], "unit": "QLIKE ÷ live σ", "note": "Stability check. 1.00 = same loss as the live σ; below 1 = better. GARCH is fitted on NY-close daily returns; its 2018 fits use about 300 bars.", "rows": [{"label": "2018", "values": [0.8742, 1.1266, 0.9673]}, {"label": "2019", "values": [0.8029, 1.1386, 0.9725]}, {"label": "2020", "values": [0.6994, 1.3838, 0.8141]}, {"label": "2021", "values": [0.7305, 1.0221, 0.96]}, {"label": "2022", "values": [0.8133, 1.0949, 0.9392]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Per instrument: log-HAR loss ÷ live σ loss", "unit": "QLIKE ÷ live σ", "ref": 1, "note": "Below 1: a model on M1 realised variance forecasts that instrument's session variance better than the live daily-bar σ. Benchmark: 1.", "rows": [{"label": "EURCHF", "value": 0.4908}, {"label": "GBPAUD", "value": 0.637}, {"label": "GBPCHF", "value": 0.6807}, {"label": "DE30", "value": 0.6877}, {"label": "EURGBP", "value": 0.6918}, {"label": "CADJPY", "value": 0.7028}, {"label": "GBPNZD", "value": 0.7075}, {"label": "GBPJPY", "value": 0.7101}, {"label": "GBPCAD", "value": 0.7239}, {"label": "GBPUSD", "value": 0.7295}, {"label": "AUDCHF", "value": 0.7362}, {"label": "AUDJPY", "value": 0.7424}, {"label": "UK100", "value": 0.7446}, {"label": "SPX500", "value": 0.7505}, {"label": "NZDJPY", "value": 0.7647}, {"label": "DOW", "value": 0.7653}, {"label": "NQ", "value": 0.7726}, {"label": "CHFJPY", "value": 0.7749}, {"label": "US2000", "value": 0.777}, {"label": "AUDNZD", "value": 0.7818}, {"label": "EURAUD", "value": 0.7937}, {"label": "EURNZD", "value": 0.8028}, {"label": "GOLD", "value": 0.8132}, {"label": "USDCHF", "value": 0.8202}, {"label": "CADCHF", "value": 0.8357}, {"label": "EURJPY", "value": 0.8466}, {"label": "USDJPY", "value": 0.8488}, {"label": "EURCAD", "value": 0.8744}, {"label": "AUDCAD", "value": 0.8943}, {"label": "AUDUSD", "value": 0.9219}, {"label": "NZDCAD", "value": 0.9497}, {"label": "EURUSD", "value": 0.9556}, {"label": "NZDUSD", "value": 0.9654}, {"label": "USDCAD", "value": 0.9704}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Expected change in vol vs what happened next week", "unit": "realised change, log vol", "xlabel": "predicted change (Δσ expected, decile means)", "note": "Realised = half log of mean RV5 over the next 5 sessions ÷ the last 5. Perfect forecast lies on the diagonal; 'no change' is the flat 0 line. Correlation 0.38 for Δσ expected vs 0.21 for plain mean reversion (−σ vs long-run). Slope 0.72.", "series": [{"name": "Δσ expected", "points": [[-0.195, -0.169], [-0.063, -0.095], [-0.02, -0.053], [0.011, -0.024], [0.038, 0.004], [0.061, 0.025], [0.084, 0.04], [0.11, 0.055], [0.142, 0.081], [0.21, 0.141]]}, {"name": "perfect", "points": [[-0.195, -0.195], [0.21, 0.21]]}, {"name": "no change", "points": [[-0.195, 0], [0.21, 0]]}]}, {"type": "bars", "title": "Which field best ranks the next loud session?", "unit": "AUC (0.5 = coin flip)", "ref": 0.5, "note": "Loud = the session's RV5 above its own trailing-year 80th percentile (threshold past-only; 24% of sessions). AUC per instrument, averaged. Benchmarks: 0.5 and σ now (the live σ).", "rows": [{"label": "σ now", "value": 0.758}, {"label": "Δσ expected", "value": 0.288}, {"label": "σ vs long-run", "value": 0.798}, {"label": "P(high regime)", "value": 0.761}, {"label": "forecast error", "value": 0.602}, {"label": "yesterday's RV", "value": 0.793}, {"label": "log-HAR forecast", "value": 0.782}]}, {"type": "lines", "title": "Real days: EURUSD, Jan-Jun 2020, the regime probability vs σ and realised vol", "unit": "see note", "xlabel": "session number from 2020-01-02", "note": "P(high regime) is the predicted probability for each session from data up to the day before. σ ÷ 1-year median and realised √RV5 ÷ σ show why it moves. Session 47 = 9 Mar 2020, 55 = 19 Mar. Benchmark: σ alone (the σ ÷ median lin